# Drafted by Gemini (R19 epilogue), edited. After the Chained Reaper: Isolde's Walk, Adela, Golub's move, Doris.

~ walk_ask
quest isolde_walk asked
Narrator: Isolde pauses in the stone doorway of the sepulcher and gently tugs the hem of your coat with her teeth. She turns her white eyes toward the dark paths among the graves, then looks back to you.
* Walk with her -> walk_yes
* Not now, old girl -> walk_no

~ walk_yes
set mm_isolde_walk_started
Narrator: Isolde trots out along the nearest gravel path with her hooded lantern swinging low, glancing back every few paces to make sure you follow.
-> END

~ walk_no
Narrator: Isolde lowers her heavy black chest onto the cold stone step and watches the fogbound path with her ears laid flat.
* Change your mind -> walk_yes
* [ends:isolde_walk] Leave her -> walk_leave

~ walk_leave
set mm_isolde_walk_gone
quest isolde_walk gone_quiet
Narrator: Isolde does not follow you past the iron gate, and by the time morning thins the mist her hooded lantern sits dark beside the sepulcher door.
-> END

~ walk_crimson
set mm_walk_crimson
set mm_isolde_walk_sites += 1
Narrator: Setting her lantern down, Isolde noses through the cold grey ash of the crimson brazier and nudges out a small wooden horse carved by Yorgrim's patient hand.
-> END

~ walk_violet
set mm_walk_violet
set mm_isolde_walk_sites += 1
Narrator: At the mossy foot of the violet fountain, Isolde sniffs the damp flagstones and paws loose a pale mask of polished bone that Yorgrim tucked away.
-> END

~ walk_emerald
set mm_walk_emerald
set mm_isolde_walk_sites += 1
Narrator: Isolde burrows her black snout beneath the knotted emerald roots and draws out a fragrant sprig of dried greenery bound with coarse thread.
-> END

~ walk_end
set mm_isolde_walk_done
quest isolde_walk done
give yorgrims_letter
Narrator: Beneath the leaning Shadestone markers, Isolde noses a flat packet wrapped in tied oilcloth out of the peat: Yorgrim's final letter to Mori Shade.
-> END

~ adela
set mm_epilogue_adela
adela_druskenvald [smile]: You have my deepest thanks for settling that dreadful business behind the cemetery iron, darlings. Honestly, I rather thought our little graveyard unpleasantness had been put to bed for good.
adela_druskenvald [sly]: Though I did spot the queerest flock of gray pigeons roosting inside the tower clockwork this evening.
-> END

~ golub_tease
set mm_epilogue_golub
Narrator: High on the slate roof of the post office, a hundred gray pigeons shift their feet as one. Below the eaves, Theodora Mayville watches you pass down the lane with gleaming violet eyes.
-> END

~ weston
set mm_epilogue_weston
weston_murdoch [smile]: The Brightsingers heard the chapel bells ring clear across the valley mist tonight, my friends. We shall gather every lantern on the steps and sing the weary dead home until dawn.
-> END

~ doris_after
set mm_epilogue_doris
doris_squire [neutral]: The lane is quiet from the iron gates to the square tonight. You have my thanks for keeping the mist off our cobbles.
-> END
